.SS "SystemEx\&.Collections\&.Generic\&.VectorFlexSpan< T, TContainer >\&.VectorFlexSpan (ref TContainer pVector, long start, \fBFlexSpanMode\fP mode)"

.PP
Creates a FlexSpan view starting at \fIstart\fP  and extending to the end of the underlying container\&. This constructor does not allocate memory\&. It simply creates a logical view over the container using the specified indexing mode\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpVector\fP \fBReference\fP to the underlying container\&. Passed by ref to avoid copying the container struct and to ensure the view always reflects the actual container\&. 
.br
\fIstart\fP The starting index of the view\&. Must be within the bounds of the container\&. 
.br
\fImode\fP Indexing mode used by the view: System = forward indexing, Reverse = backward indexing, Ring = circular wrap-around indexing\&. 
.RE
.PP

